## R. Hostile review of this map (2026-07-31) — corrections applied below

This section records **weaknesses, inconsistencies, and fixes** found when checking the map against trunk architecture. Numbered items marked **FIXED IN MAP** were applied in §§1–10 of this revision (`rev: 2`).

### R.1 Critical — DG-1 “host kit” vs handler ownership (architecture clash)

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Clash | Trunk already mandates `httpRoutes.loadHandlersFromPackage: true` and `handlerPackage: @app-tour/workspace-<id>/host/http`. Handlers are **workspace-owned**, dispatched via codegen. |
| Map error (rev1) | “Lift catalog/registration HTTP skeleton to platform” read like moving handlers into `apps/api` / `platform-core`. That **violates** P5/P8 and guest API shell guards. |
| **Correction** | Split **P** into **P-contract** (SDK shapes, ports) and **P-lib** (shared pure/helpers package **imported by** workspace handlers). Workspaces keep thin `handleGet*`; duplication dies inside W packages via shared lib — not by host owning product HTTP. |
| Kit home (OD-2) | Prefer new `@app-tour/workspace-guest-http` (or sdk subpath) **or** shared module under an existing neutral package. **Do not** dump HTTP handlers into `platform-core` (wizard host already lives there; different concern). |

### R.2 Critical — “Config-only second product” overclaims

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Overclaim | Mountain (itinerary, gear, photos) vs city (venue, capacity) is not expressible as theme+flags alone; field registry / validation / composites remain **W**. |
| Honest north star | Second product = **C (manifest) + thin W adapters + P-lib**. Not “JSON only”. |
| Clone detector still valid | Parallel *rename forests* are the smell; legitimate small W modules are not. |

### R.3 High — Guest slice ≠ full product (DG-4 under-scoped for “product #2”)

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Gap | DG-4 only proves marketing catalog → portal register. Denali production shape also includes admin wizard depth, finance, booking, L4 member portal. |
| Urban today | L3 guest + `memberPortal.availability: minimal` — intentionally not Denali. |
| **Correction** | Introduce **product maturity ladder** (G0→G3). DG-4 exits at **G1 (guest-viable stub)**. “Second certified product” at DG-5 must declare which rung (guest-only certified vs operator-complete). Do not equate G1 with Denali parity. |

**Maturity ladder (normative):**

| Rung | Name | Minimum | Typical tier |
| ---- | ---- | ------- | ------------ |
| G0 | Scaffold | manifest + theme + codegen loads | stub |
| G1 | Guest-viable | catalog HTTP + registration + landing/SEO + smoke | stub (DG-4 exit) |
| G2 | Operator-viable | tour-write + publish + minimal admin create/list | stub or certified (Architect) |
| G3 | Reference-class | wizard depth and/or finance/booking + L4 member as required by product | certified |

Denali today ≈ **G3**. Urban today ≈ **G1−** (guest pieces present, still mirror-shaped). Path B success ≠ cloning G3.

### R.4 High — Urban as DG-4 vehicle conflicts with Phase 7 intent

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Phase 7 | Urban is **starter-plus proof of genericity**, explicitly *not* a second Denali (`URBAN-MINIMAL-SCOPE.md`). |
| Risk of 1a | “Rebuild Urban into product #2” blurs proof workspace with commercial product; can regress Phase 7 contract (“zero urban-specific platform-core PRs”). |
| **Correction** | Default OD-1 → **1b** (new `pluginId` for product #2). Keep `urban` as permanent **proof/stub** unless Architect explicitly re-charters Phase 7. Option 1a only with written Phase 7 amendment. |

### R.5 High — Sequencing thrash (DG-1 ∥ DG-3 on same files)

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Rev1 | Allowed DG-3 peel of Denali HTTP in parallel with DG-1 Urban rewire of the same patterns. |
| Risk | Two PRs rewrite the same stems twice; merge conflict + behavior drift on certified Denali. |
| **Correction** | **Serialize extract:** (1) extract P-lib from *one* reference (prefer Denali or a third shared module), (2) switch Urban **or** guest-club first (non-certified), (3) only then peel Denali onto P-lib (DG-3 P0). DG-3 P0 **blocked** until DG-1 consumer #1 green. |

### R.6 High — Finance gravity is a separate axis (underweighted)

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Fact | Shared `@app-tour/finance-http` exists; **route group registration still hangs on Denali manifest** (`FINANCE_WORKSPACE_ONBOARDING_LIFECYCLE.md`). finance-ws* are registry fixtures, not products. |
| Map gap | DG-1 catalog kit does not fix “second product with finance”. |
| **Correction** | Add explicit track **DG-F** (optional, after G2): finance route registration becomes platform/capability-owned (or any `workspaceFinance.supported: true` workspace can declare the shared finance-http group), not Denali-only. Default for Path B G1: **finance out of scope**. |

### R.7 Medium — Already-shared pieces understated (false greenfield)

Rev1 treated shared kits as net-new. Trunk already has:

| Existing shared piece | Implication for DG-1 |
| --------------------- | -------------------- |
| `catalogRegistrationFlow` compose + `reuseAuthStepsFrom: "shared"` | Portal registration **steps** already shared — do not rebuild |
| `defineCatalogRegistrationFlowSurface` / SDK registration registry | Extend; don’t fork |
| `createPlatformWizardHostHooks` (urban + starter) | Wizard host lift partially done — DG-3 P1 is continuation, not invention |
| Manifest `httpRoutes` codegen + lazy handler loaders | Host dispatch is already generic — duplication is **inside** W packages |
| `@app-tour/finance-http` | Pattern to copy for guest HTTP P-lib (shared impl, W re-export/adapters) |

**Correction:** DG-1 = **collapse W-level rename clones onto P-lib**, not invent a second registration platform.

### R.8 Medium — First consumer should be lowest-risk stub

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Rev1 | “Wire Urban first”. |
| Risk | Urban carries Phase 7 semantics + more HTTP surface; breakage looks like product regression. |
| **Correction** | Prefer **guest-club** (or a throwaway spike workspace) as **first** P-lib consumer; Urban second; Denali third (DG-3). |

### R.9 Medium — Starter `aliasCatalogWorkspaceType: "denali"` misplaced in DG-1

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Risk | Removing alias before a **neutral field/wizard catalog** exists breaks starter wizard scaffold. |
| **Correction** | Move to **DG-2** exit (requires substitute catalog). DG-1 must not depend on breaking the alias. |

### R.10 Medium — Weak success metric (“≪ 10% of Denali LOC”)

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Why weak | Urban is already ~8.6% of full Denali LOC while still a clone structurally. Absolute LOC ratio does not measure clone-ness. |
| **Correction** | Primary metrics: (1) parallel stem count for shared patterns → 0, (2) new W files for G1 slice below budget (e.g. ≤15 adapter files), (3) no new `src/http` forest. LOC ratio optional only vs **Denali guest-equivalent subset**, not whole Denali. |

### R.11 Medium — Certification rules already exist; map must align

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Phase H | `certified` needs L3+; with `memberApp: true` needs L4. Default omitted tier = stub. |
| Map | DG-5 must choose: guest-only product (`memberApp` false, L3 certified) vs Denali-like L4. |
| **Correction** | OD-5 added. Do not assume product #2 needs `memberApp: true`. |

### R.12 Medium — Doc-first covenant under-specified

| Issue | Detail |
| ----- | ------ |
| Rule | Changes to `platform-core` / `workspace-sdk` / `apps/api` require Markdoc update in `docs/` before code (`guard-docs` / .cursorrules). |
| **Correction** | Each DG phase that touches protected packages opens with **doc PR / Markdoc section** (even if SOT still TEMP-promoted). TEMP map alone does **not** satisfy `guard-docs` on commit. |

### R.13 Low — Path A regression not checklisted

DG work on shared libs can break Denali catalog/registration. **Correction:** every DG-1/DG-3 PR lists Path A smoke: Denali guest catalog + register + (if touched) finance summary path — fast-track only.

### R.14 Low — Consistency with saas-platform-remediation (DONE)

That charter closed thin-shell / host allowlist. Gravity map must **not** re-open “move Denali UI into apps” or grow allowlists. Aligns if P-lib is workspace-importable shared code and apps stay loader-only.

### R.15 Open product question (not a map bug)

Is “product #2” a **city-event vertical** (Urban semantics, G2) or a **second outdoor club brand** (would be Path A / config on Denali)? If the business need is only second brand, **Path B is the wrong program** — cancel after DG-0 Option 2.

