## 1. North star (rev 2 — honest)

```text
Second product family (Path B)
  = C (manifest/profile) + thin W adapters + P-lib/P-contract
  ≠ fork/rename of packages/workspaces/denali
  ≠ “JSON-only” with zero W code
  ≠ Denali G3 parity on day one (ladder G1 → G2 → optional G3)
```

### Ownership rule (rev 2)

| Bucket | Owner | May contain | Must not contain |
| ------ | ----- | ----------- | ---------------- |
| **P-contract** | `workspace-sdk` (+ codegen) | Ports, surface types, registration compose contracts | Product field lists, Denali UI |
| **P-lib** | Neutral shared package (OD-2) | Reusable catalog/registration HTTP helpers, mappers used by ≥2 workspaces | `pluginId` branches; apps/api handlers |
| **C** | `workspace.manifest.json` | Routes prefixes, presentation flags, theme, SEO, capabilities, tier | Executable business rules |
| **W** | `packages/workspaces/<id>` | Thin handlers calling P-lib; domain schema/UI/rules/finance policy | Copy-paste forests of another workspace |

### Clone detector (rev 2)

**FAIL** if G1 onboarding adds a large rename-parallel tree (`*-catalog.service`, `*-registration.service`, …) instead of P-lib calls.

**PASS** if G1 is mostly C + ≤ budget adapter files + P-lib.


