## 4. Phase map (DG-0 … DG-6 + DG-F) — rev 2

### Dependency graph (serialized where required)

```text
DG-0 doctrine + OD-1/2/5 lock + Path A vs B confirmation
        │
        ├─► DG-1 P-lib extract + consumer #1 (guest-club or spike)
        │         │
        │         ├─► consumer #2 (urban proof rewire) —— still stub
        │         │
        │         └─► DG-3 P0 Denali peel onto P-lib  [BLOCKED until consumer #1 green]
        │
        ├─► DG-2 config/catalog neutrality (∥ late DG-1; owns starter alias break)
        │
        └─► DG-4 G1 product #2 proof (new pluginId default)  [needs DG-1 + DG-2]
                  │
                  ├─► (optional) G2 operator-viable slice
                  │
                  ▼
             DG-5 certify at agreed rung (OD-5)
                  │
                  ├─► DG-F finance registration neutrality (optional; G2+ only)
                  │
                  ▼
             DG-6 cleanup / clone-detector ratchet
```

**Hard rules (rev 2)**

1. Do **not** start DG-4 before DG-1 has ≥1 non-Denali consumer on P-lib.
2. Do **not** start DG-3 P0 (Denali HTTP peel) before that consumer is green.
3. Do **not** break starter Denali catalog alias in DG-1 — that is DG-2.
4. Do **not** treat DG-4 G1 as Denali parity.
5. Default product #2 vehicle = **new pluginId (1b)**; Urban stays Phase 7 proof.

**Parallel safe:** DG-2 ∥ late DG-1; DG-3 P1/P2 (wizard/seeds) ∥ DG-4 after P0 policy clear; DG-F only after finance in scope.

